<title>USA: US Stockpile sells antimony, no cadmium awards.</title>
<headline>US Stockpile sells antimony, no cadmium awards.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 55,423 pounds of antimony to AMSPEC Chemical Corp of Pennsylvania for an approximate current market value of $56,000.</p>
<p>The stockpile made no award for cadmium.</p>
<p>The next receipt of offers for antimony and cadmium will be March 11.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
